  {:business/id :kbb-migration
   :business/name "KBB migration"
   :business/repo "kotoba-lang/kotoba"
   :business/what
   "Evolve the existing fail-closed `bin/kbb` bootstrap into the workspace's
    Kotoba-authored automation path, then migrate nbb and bb scripts in
    dependency order. The current command is explicitly `:bootstrap-jvm`;
    native self-hosting and script-parity remain separate qualification gates."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :qa]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :product-manager
     :why "This is a bounded runtime-and-migration program. The director owns dependency order and acceptance boundaries; a second prioritization role would duplicate that decision."}
    {:role :designer
     :why "The first deliverable is a CLI/runtime compatibility contract, not a human-facing interface."}
    {:role :sales
     :why "This internal migration has no named prospect or buying decision."}
    {:role :marketer
     :why "There is no public KBB release to promote until runtime and parity evidence exist."}
    {:role :supporter
     :why "There are no KBB users until a qualified executable surface exists."}
    {:role :financial-chief
     :why "The migration has no independent revenue, pricing, or funds-moving responsibility."}]
   :business/job-focus
   {:director
    "Start from the observed boundary: `bin/kbb` accepts only `.kotoba` plus an explicit no-wildcard policy, hosts exact scoped `:fs/app-data`, records capability receipts, and reports `nbb-loaded? false`; it is still JVM-bootstrapped. Choose one dependency-ordered outcome: packaging, one real hosted capability with denial tests, compatibility inventory, or one proven script migration."
    :engineer
    "Extend `kbb` one capability slice at a time with a real provider and denial tests; never add a ClojureScript or nbb fallback. Convert at most one nbb/bb script per run, preserving argv, cwd, environment, stdout, stderr, exit status, and filesystem effects. Keep the old entrypoint until differential proof passes."
   :qa
    "Falsify the KBB safety boundary before compatibility: reject `.cljs`, wildcard resources, unhosted capabilities, and out-of-scope writes; require receipts and `nbb-loaded? false`. For migration, compare the same script, inputs, environment, and machine across stdout, stderr, exit status, and filesystem effects. Unsupported host APIs are BLOCKED, not equivalent."}}

  {:business/id :kotobascript
   :business/name "KotobaScript"
   :business/repo "kotoba-lang/amu"
   :business/what
   "Make Kotoba source compile and run as JavaScript through Amu with a
    ClojureScript-like developer experience. Build on the existing
    `:cljs-kotoba-v1` source backend and restricted `--target js` ESM backend;
    neither backend alone proves a named, end-to-end KotobaScript surface."
   :business/roles [:director :engineer :qa]
   :business/roles-absent
   [{:role :product-manager
     :why "This is a bounded language/runtime program. The director owns the compatibility envelope and slice order until an external product surface exists."}
    {:role :designer
     :why "The first interface is a compiler and executable module contract, not a visual UI."}
    {:role :sales
     :why "There is no named buyer or commercial KotobaScript offering yet."}
    {:role :marketer
     :why "A public claim must wait for reproducible Node and browser execution evidence."}
    {:role :supporter
     :why "There are no supported KotobaScript users until the executable contract and diagnostics are released."}
    {:role :financial-chief
     :why "The language target has no independent pricing, revenue, or funds-moving responsibility."}]
   :business/job-focus
   {:director
    "Define the smallest honest KotobaScript contract across source syntax, namespaces, modules, standard library, host capabilities, Node/browser execution, diagnostics, and source maps. Reuse Amu's existing cljs and restricted-JS backends where they fit; do not rename either backend and call the whole surface complete."
    :engineer
    "Deliver one end-to-end slice at a time: accepted Kotoba source, Amu lowering, deterministic JavaScript or ESM artifact, and real Node or browser execution without a JVM, nbb, or a ClojureScript compiler at runtime. Keep capabilities deny-by-default and preserve typed-value, fuel, overflow, module-graph, and export gates."
    :qa
    "Try to falsify KotobaScript with real generated artifacts. Compare the same supported program across the current Amu reference path and Node/browser execution, including values, stdout, errors, exit status, deterministic bytes, capability denial, and source locations. Unsupported ClojureScript semantics are explicit gaps, never silent compatibility."}}

